PURPOSE
H8 established that slow representational rank can be treated as an adaptive resource.

H9 asks the structural analogue of H5:

How long must off-manifold novelty persist before it should allocate a permanent slow degree of freedom?

Desired:

brief novelty
->
fast adaptation / expression override only.

persistent reusable novelty
->
slow structural growth.

return after brief novelty
->
old compact inherited structure remains intact.

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- prove a real Yggdrasil structural-write timescale;
- freeze a persistence threshold;
- prove real developmental novelty is linear;
- replace fast phenotype adaptation with slow memory;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

