PRIMARY TRADEOFF
Longer persistence gating reduces accidental permanent growth,
but delays the benefit of real reusable structure.

Therefore:

STRUCTURAL FIDELITY
vs
STRUCTURAL ADAPTATION LATENCY

is a genuine tradeoff.

There is no universal persistence constant in this toy.

POST-NOVELTY PRUNING
For the primary 5-block gate,
when rank 2 had been allocated,
median pruning latency after return to rank-1 conditions is approximately:

300 to 400 observations.

Post-return learned loss is approximately:

0.0498 to 0.0499

for the persistent conditions.

Thus growth is reversible,
but not instantaneous.

This creates a short structural hangover.

IMPORTANT NEGATIVE
At D=300:

fixed rank 2:
0.11762

persistence-gated structural memory:
0.14651.

The conservative memory policy knowingly gives up temporary performance.

That is not an implementation bug.

It expresses the design goal:

DO NOT TURN EVERY TEMPORARILY USEFUL ADAPTATION
INTO PERMANENT HEREDITARY STRUCTURE.

Fast phenotype adaptation must carry more of the short-lived burden.

RELATION TO H3 / H6
H3:
current local utility should override inherited bias.

H6:
stale inherited expression can be suppressed before slow state is erased.

H9:
novel current function can be expressed before slow representational capacity is expanded.

This produces a consistent ordering:

FAST PHENOTYPE FIRST.

SLOW HEREDITY ONLY AFTER PERSISTENCE.

RELATION TO H5
H5 asked:

when should repeated useful action direction write a slow prior?

H9 asks:

when should repeated useful unexplained structure allocate an additional slow degree of freedom?

Both use the same abstract criterion:

PERSISTENT USEFULNESS
NOT
IMMEDIATE USEFULNESS.

RELATION TO H7/H8
H7:
insufficient rank can become harmful,
so off-manifold evidence must reduce inherited expression trust.

H8:
persistent reusable off-manifold structure can justify rank growth.

H9:
the transition between those responses should be persistence-gated.

Therefore the full response to off-manifold novelty becomes:

FIRST:
reduce trust in current inherited manifold.

SECOND:
use fast/direct adaptation.

THIRD:
accumulate evidence that the residual is persistent and reusable.

FOURTH:
grow permanent structure only if value persists.

RETURN:
prune only after persistent evidence that the added structure is no longer worth its cost.

STRUCTURAL WRITE CONFIDENCE
H9 suggests that structural memory needs its own confidence variable.

Do not collapse:

SLOW VALUE WRITE CONFIDENCE

with

SLOW STRUCTURAL-GROWTH CONFIDENCE.

A regime may repeatedly favor the same prior within existing capacity,
or
it may require genuinely new representational capacity.

Those are different slow-memory operations.

CURRENT SLOW-MEMORY STACK

INHERITED MANIFOLD

+

